IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `lsl-dates`
IMPORT `lsl-rules`

-- Long Service Leave Act 2018 (Vic) -- the questions of the EMPLOYEE.
--
-- SEAT: the employee (or former employee) to whom the Act gives long service leave, and, for the one question s 10 asks of
-- them, the personal representative of an employee who died. "Does the Act apply to me?", "From when does my employment
-- count?", "Is my employment continuous despite this absence?", "Am I entitled to long service leave yet, and how much?",
-- "What is my ordinary pay?", "Must my employer grant my request?", "What must I be paid when my employment ends, and by
-- when?", "By when must I sue?". The employer, the Industrial Division of the Magistrates' Court, the Workforce
-- Inspectorate Victoria and authorised officers get no seat: the court's opinions and satisfactions, and the employer's
-- reasonable business grounds, are asked as facts.
--
-- Every question takes plain facts (yes/no, numbers, dates, a choice from a list) and calls the rules of lsl-rules.l4. The
-- rules with deadlines (s 9(2), s 26(4), (5)) are DEONTIC rules run inside; no question takes a DEONTIC or an EVENT.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL VERSION: quotations from a plain-text conversion by Legalese Commons of the Word file of the Long Service
-- Leave Act 2018, Version No. 006 (12 December 2025), not the authorised version. (c) State of Victoria; published with
-- the authority of the Government Printer for the State of Victoria. No part may be reproduced except in accordance with
-- the Copyright Act 1968 (Cth). Quoted under the owner's ruling of 24 October 2026 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Long service leave in Victoria: the employee's questions`

§§ `Does the Act apply to me (ss 3, 5)`

@export Does Victoria's Long Service Leave Act 2018 apply to me (ss 3, 5)? It covers employees working for hire or reward in Victoria, including apprentices, casual and seasonal employees, public sector employees and police, unless another long service leave scheme takes its place.
GIVEN `I am an employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are employed to do work for hire or reward (including as an apprentice, casual or seasonal employee), or are a Victorian public sector employee, a director of a public entity, a police officer or a police reservist
      `another Victorian Act gives me long service leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether another Victorian Act gives you long service leave
      `the court considers my agreement more favourable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Industrial Division of the Magistrates' Court is of the opinion that your employment agreement (including an award or enterprise agreement) gives more favourable long service leave than the Act; answer no if no such opinion has been given
      `my employer was exempted under the 1992 Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer was exempted from Division 6 of Part 5 of the Long Service Leave Act 1992 under section 65 of that Act
      `I am employed under the Education and Training Reform Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are employed under Part 2.3, 2.4 or 2A.1 of the Education and Training Reform Act 2006 (for example as a teacher in a government school)
      `the construction industry scheme covers me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are entitled under the Construction Industry Long Service Leave Act 1997 to long service leave and to be paid benefits out of its fund
GIVETH A MAYBE `How the Act applies to me`
`Does the Act apply to me` MEANS
    `s 5 -- how the Act applies` `I am an employee` `another Victorian Act gives me long service leave` `the court considers my agreement more favourable` `my employer was exempted under the 1992 Act` `I am employed under the Education and Training Reform Act` `the construction industry scheme covers me`

§§ `Continuous employment with one employer (ss 11 to 14)`

@export From what day is my employment with my present employer counted for long service leave under Victoria's Long Service Leave Act 2018 (s 11)? Work for a related company, for an earlier owner of the business, or for an employer whose assets or work passed to your present employer can count as work for one employer.
GIVEN `the situation` IS A `Why earlier employment might count` @desc Why earlier employment might count: there is no earlier employer or business; your earlier employer was a related body corporate, or had substantially the same directors or management; the business changed owner and your employment continued; the old owner dismissed you and the new owner re-employed you on the same or substantially the same work; the assets you worked with were transferred and the new owner continued your employment; you were dismissed, the assets you worked with were transferred, and the new employer employed you to work with them or similar assets; or your work was contracted out and you moved to the contractor as a consequence
      `the day I first started` IS A DATE @desc The day you first started work at the business, or with the earlier employer (the same as the next answer if there is no earlier employer)
      `the day I started with my present employer` IS A DATE @desc The day you started work with your present employer
      `the day I was dismissed` IS A DATE @desc If you were dismissed by the old owner or employer, the day of the dismissal (otherwise any day)
      `the day I was re-employed` IS A DATE @desc If you were dismissed, the day the new owner or employer employed you (otherwise any day)
GIVETH A DATE
`From what day is my employment counted` MEANS
    `s 11 -- the day my employment with the one employer is counted from` `the situation` `the day I first started` `the day I started with my present employer` `the day I was dismissed` `the day I was re-employed`

@export Is my employment continuous for long service leave despite an absence from work, under Victoria's Long Service Leave Act 2018 (s 12)? Leave, stand-downs, industrial disputes, transfers of a business's assets, and re-employment within 12 weeks (52 after an apprenticeship) keep employment continuous; whether the absence also counts towards the length is a separate question (ss 13, 14).
GIVEN `the absence` IS A `Kind of absence` @desc What the absence was: annual leave; long service leave; parental leave; carer's leave; leave on account of illness or injury; other leave your employment agreement provides for; a gap between engagements as a casual or seasonal employee; your employer ended or interrupted your employment to avoid long service leave; the transfer of assets you usually work with to another employer; your employment was terminated by your employer or by you, and you were re-employed; your fixed-term contract expired, and you were re-employed; your apprenticeship was completed, and you were re-employed; a stand-down during industrial action; a stand-down because of a breakdown of machinery or equipment; a stand-down because of a stoppage of work; an interruption arising from an industrial dispute; or another absence
      `I am casual or seasonal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a casual or seasonal employee
      `weeks of the absence` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks the absence lasted (fractions allowed)
      `why the gap` IS A `Why the gap between engagements` @desc For a casual or seasonal gap of more than 12 weeks, why it happened: your employer and you agreed before it started that it would not break your employment; it was due to the terms of your engagement; it was caused by seasonal factors; you had been employed on a regular and systematic basis and reasonably expected to be re-engaged; or none of these
      `the day my employment ended` IS A DATE @desc If your employment was terminated, a fixed term expired or an apprenticeship was completed, the day it ended (otherwise any day)
      `the day I was re-employed` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day the same employer re-employed you (otherwise any day)
      `I could not be usefully employed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a stand-down, whether you could not be usefully employed because of the industrial action, breakdown or stoppage
      `the employer cannot reasonably be held responsible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a stand-down because of a breakdown or stoppage, whether your employer cannot reasonably be held responsible for it (a question for the court if disputed)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is my employment continuous despite the absence` MEANS
    `s 12 -- my employment is continuous despite the absence` `the absence` `I am casual or seasonal` `weeks of the absence` `why the gap` `the day my employment ended` `the day I was re-employed` `I could not be usefully employed` `the employer cannot reasonably be held responsible`

@export Was the action I was stood down during "industrial action" under Victoria's Long Service Leave Act 2018 (s 12(9), (10))? A stand-down during industrial action keeps employment continuous only if it really was industrial action.
GIVEN `the action` IS A `Kind of action` @desc What the action was: employees performing work differently so that it is restricted, limited or delayed; a ban, limitation or restriction on performing, accepting or offering for work; employees failing or refusing to attend for work or to perform any work; an employer preventing employees from working without terminating their contracts; or none of these
      `the other side authorised or agreed to it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer authorised or agreed to the employees' action (or the employees authorised or agreed to the employer's action)
      `it was based on a reasonable concern about an imminent risk to health or safety` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For employees' action, whether it was based on their reasonable concern about an imminent risk to their health or safety
      `the employee did not unreasonably refuse other safe and appropriate work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For employees' action, whether they did not unreasonably refuse an employer's direction to do other available work that was safe and appropriate
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Was it industrial action` MEANS
    `s 12(9), (10) -- it is industrial action` `the action` `the other side authorised or agreed to it` `it was based on a reasonable concern about an imminent risk to health or safety` `the employee did not unreasonably refuse other safe and appropriate work`

@export How many weeks of an absence count towards the length of my continuous employment for long service leave under Victoria's Long Service Leave Act 2018 (ss 13, 14)? Paid leave counts in full; unpaid leave counts up to 52 weeks unless an agreement says otherwise or it is for illness or injury; gaps between jobs, stand-downs and industrial disputes do not count.
GIVEN `the absence` IS A `Kind of absence` @desc What the absence was: annual leave; long service leave; parental leave; carer's leave; leave on account of illness or injury; other leave your employment agreement provides for; a gap between engagements as a casual or seasonal employee; your employer ended or interrupted your employment to avoid long service leave; the transfer of assets you usually work with to another employer; your employment was terminated by your employer or by you, and you were re-employed; your fixed-term contract expired, and you were re-employed; your apprenticeship was completed, and you were re-employed; a stand-down during industrial action; a stand-down because of a breakdown of machinery or equipment; a stand-down because of a stoppage of work; an interruption arising from an industrial dispute; or another absence
      `it was paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the leave was paid leave
      `weeks of the absence` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks the absence lasted (fractions allowed)
      `my employment agreement counts it as employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employment agreement (including an award or enterprise agreement) says the absence counts as employment
      `we agreed in writing before the leave that it counts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer and you agreed in writing, before the leave was taken, that it counts as employment
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`How many weeks of the absence count` MEANS
    `ss 13, 14 -- the weeks of the absence that count` `the absence` `it was paid` `weeks of the absence` `my employment agreement counts it as employment` `we agreed in writing before the leave that it counts`

@export Does my apprenticeship count towards my continuous employment for long service leave under Victoria's Long Service Leave Act 2018 (s 13(2))? It counts if you enter a contract of employment with the same employer within 52 weeks after completing it.
GIVEN `the day my apprenticeship was completed` IS A DATE @desc The day you completed your apprenticeship
      `the day I entered the contract` IS A DATE @desc The day you entered a contract of employment with the same employer
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does my apprenticeship count` MEANS
    `s 13(2) -- my apprenticeship counts` `the day my apprenticeship was completed` `the day I entered the contract`

§§ `My entitlement (ss 6, 7, 8)`

@export Am I entitled to long service leave yet under Victoria's Long Service Leave Act 2018 (s 6)? You are entitled at any time after completing 7 years of continuous employment with one employer.
GIVEN `the day it is counted from` IS A DATE @desc The day your continuous employment with your employer is counted from (see the question on the day your employment is counted from)
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE @desc The day you are asking about (today, or the last day of your employment), counted as a day of employment
      `weeks that do not count` IS A NUMBER @desc The total weeks of absence that do not count towards the length of your employment (the absence questions give, for each absence, the weeks that count; the rest do not); 0 if none
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Am I entitled to long service leave yet` MEANS
    `yes or no` (`s 6 -- I have completed 7 years` `the day it is counted from` `the day asked about` `weeks that do not count`)

@export How many weeks of long service leave am I entitled to under Victoria's Long Service Leave Act 2018 (s 6)? After 7 years of continuous employment, 1/60th of the whole period of continuous employment (about 6.1 weeks after 7 years, 8.7 after 10), less the long service leave already taken; none before 7 years.
GIVEN `the day it is counted from` IS A DATE @desc The day your continuous employment with your employer is counted from (see the question on the day your employment is counted from)
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE @desc The day you are asking about (today, or the last day of your employment), counted as a day of employment
      `weeks that do not count` IS A NUMBER @desc The total weeks of absence that do not count towards the length of your employment; 0 if none
      `weeks already taken` IS A NUMBER @desc The weeks of long service leave you have already taken in the period (including leave taken in advance); 0 if none
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How many weeks of long service leave am I entitled to` MEANS
    `s 6 -- the weeks of long service leave` `the day it is counted from` `the day asked about` `weeks that do not count` `weeks already taken`

@export How many weeks of my long service leave does a period of leave use under Victoria's Long Service Leave Act 2018 (s 7)? Public holidays and annual leave falling within the period are not long service leave.
GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE @desc The first day of the period of leave
      `the last day` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the period of leave
      `public holidays` IS A NUMBER @desc How many public holidays fall within the period
      `days of annual leave` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days of annual leave you take within the period
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How many weeks of long service leave does the period use` MEANS
    `s 7 -- the weeks of long service leave the period uses` `the first day` `the last day` `public holidays` `days of annual leave`

@export I took long service leave in advance and my employment is ending: how much of the pay for it can my employer deduct from my final pay under Victoria's Long Service Leave Act 2018 (s 8(3))? The employer may deduct the pay for the advance leave you never became entitled to.
GIVEN `the day it is counted from` IS A DATE @desc The day your continuous employment with your employer is counted from
      `the last day` IS A DATE @desc The day your employment ends
      `weeks that do not count` IS A NUMBER @desc The total weeks of absence that do not count towards the length of your employment; 0 if none
      `other weeks already taken` IS A NUMBER @desc Weeks of long service leave you took after becoming entitled (not in advance); 0 if none
      `weeks of leave taken in advance` IS A NUMBER @desc Weeks of long service leave your employer let you take before you were entitled to it
      `the amount paid for it` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount, in dollars, you were paid for the leave taken in advance
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much of my advance leave pay can be deducted` MEANS
    `s 8(3) -- the most that may be deducted` `weeks of leave taken in advance` `the amount paid for it` (`s 6 -- the weeks of long service leave` `the day it is counted from` `the last day` `weeks that do not count` `other weeks already taken`)

§§ `My pay for long service leave (ss 15, 16, 17)`

@export What is my weekly ordinary pay for long service leave under Victoria's Long Service Leave Act 2018 (s 15)? Your normal weekly hours at your ordinary time rate of pay; if no rate is fixed, the greatest of your average weekly earnings over the last 52 weeks, the last 260 weeks and your whole period of employment; plus the cash value of any board or lodging.
GIVEN `my rate is fixed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employment agreement (including an award or enterprise agreement) fixes an ordinary time rate of pay for your work
      `my normal weekly hours` IS A NUMBER @desc Your normal weekly hours (see the question on normal weekly hours if they are not fixed or have changed)
      `my hourly rate` IS A NUMBER @desc Your fixed ordinary time rate of pay, in dollars an hour, on the day the leave starts (0 if not fixed)
      `average weekly earnings over 52 weeks` IS A NUMBER @desc If no rate is fixed, your average weekly earnings, in dollars, in the 52 weeks before the leave starts (0 otherwise)
      `average weekly earnings over 260 weeks` IS A NUMBER @desc If no rate is fixed, your average weekly earnings, in dollars, in the 260 weeks before the leave starts (0 otherwise)
      `average weekly earnings over the whole period` IS A NUMBER @desc If no rate is fixed, your average weekly earnings, in dollars, over your whole period of continuous employment before the leave starts (0 otherwise)
      `weekly cash value of board or lodging` IS A NUMBER @desc The weekly cash value, in dollars, of any board or lodging your employer gives you (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my weekly ordinary pay` MEANS
    `s 15 -- my weekly ordinary pay` `my rate is fixed` `my normal weekly hours` `my hourly rate` `average weekly earnings over 52 weeks` `average weekly earnings over 260 weeks` `average weekly earnings over the whole period` `weekly cash value of board or lodging`

@export What are my normal weekly hours for long service leave under Victoria's Long Service Leave Act 2018 (s 16)? If no hours are fixed, or your fixed hours changed in the 104 weeks before the leave, they are the greatest of three averages: over the last 52 weeks, the last 260 weeks, and your last period of continuous employment, each counting paid leave hours as hours worked and leaving out weeks of unpaid leave.
GIVEN `my hours are fixed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employment agreement fixes a normal weekly number of hours
      `my fixed weekly hours` IS A NUMBER @desc Your fixed normal weekly hours (0 if not fixed)
      `my hours changed in the last 104 weeks` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your fixed hours changed one or more times in the 104 weeks before the leave starts
      `hours worked in 52 weeks` IS A NUMBER @desc Hours you worked in the 52 weeks before the leave starts
      `paid leave hours in 52 weeks` IS A NUMBER @desc Hours of paid leave you took in those 52 weeks
      `unpaid leave weeks in 52 weeks` IS A NUMBER @desc Weeks of unpaid leave you took in those 52 weeks
      `hours worked in 260 weeks` IS A NUMBER @desc Hours you worked in the 260 weeks before the leave starts
      `paid leave hours in 260 weeks` IS A NUMBER @desc Hours of paid leave you took in those 260 weeks
      `unpaid leave weeks in 260 weeks` IS A NUMBER @desc Weeks of unpaid leave you took in those 260 weeks
      `hours worked in the whole period` IS A NUMBER @desc Hours you worked in your last period of continuous employment before the leave starts
      `paid leave hours in the whole period` IS A NUMBER @desc Hours of paid leave you took in that period
      `weeks of the whole period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks that period lasted
      `unpaid leave weeks in the whole period` IS A NUMBER @desc Weeks of unpaid leave you took in that period
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What are my normal weekly hours` MEANS
    `s 16 -- my normal weekly hours` `my hours are fixed` `my fixed weekly hours` `my hours changed in the last 104 weeks` `hours worked in 52 weeks` `paid leave hours in 52 weeks` `unpaid leave weeks in 52 weeks` `hours worked in 260 weeks` `paid leave hours in 260 weeks` `unpaid leave weeks in 260 weeks` `hours worked in the whole period` `paid leave hours in the whole period` `weeks of the whole period` `unpaid leave weeks in the whole period`

@export I am on WorkCover weekly payments or in suitable employment after a workplace injury: what weekly pay is my long service leave worked out on under Victoria's Long Service Leave Act 2018 (s 17)? The greater of your hours and rate just before the leave and just before the injury or illness.
GIVEN `s 17 applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are working in suitable employment under the Workplace Injury Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2013, or absent because of a workplace illness or injury and receiving weekly payments of compensation from WorkSafe Victoria
      `hours before the leave` IS A NUMBER @desc Your normal weekly hours immediately before the leave starts
      `rate before the leave` IS A NUMBER @desc Your ordinary time rate of pay, in dollars an hour, immediately before the leave starts
      `hours before the injury` IS A NUMBER @desc Your normal weekly hours immediately before the injury or illness
      `rate before the injury` IS A NUMBER @desc Your ordinary time rate of pay, in dollars an hour, immediately before the injury or illness
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What weekly pay is my leave worked out on after a workplace injury` MEANS
    `s 17 -- my weekly pay on the hours and rate taken` `s 17 applies` `hours before the leave` `rate before the leave` `hours before the injury` `rate before the injury`

§§ `Taking my leave (ss 18 to 22)`

@export Must my employer grant my request to take long service leave under Victoria's Long Service Leave Act 2018 (s 18)? You may ask for a period of at least 1 day; your employer must grant it as soon as practicable unless it has reasonable business grounds for refusing.
GIVEN `days requested` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days of long service leave you asked for
      `I have long service leave to take` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are entitled to long service leave not yet taken
      `the employer has reasonable business grounds` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer has reasonable business grounds for refusing, such as no capacity, or it being impractical, to change other employees' arrangements or recruit, a likely significant loss of efficiency or productivity, or a likely significant negative impact on customer service (the court decides if disputed)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must my employer grant my request for leave` MEANS
    `s 18 -- my employer must grant my request` `days requested` `I have long service leave to take` `the employer has reasonable business grounds`

@export My employer has directed me to take long service leave: must I take it under Victoria's Long Service Leave Act 2018 (s 19)? Yes, if the direction gave you at least 12 weeks' written notice, unless the Industrial Division of the Magistrates' Court orders otherwise.
GIVEN `the notice was written` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the direction was given to you in writing
      `the day notice was given` IS A DATE @desc The day you were given the notice
      `the day the leave starts` IS A DATE @desc The day the directed leave is to start
      `the court has ordered otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Industrial Division of the Magistrates' Court has made an order that you need not comply
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must I take leave when directed` MEANS
    `s 19 -- I must comply with the direction` `the notice was written` `the day notice was given` `the day the leave starts` `the court has ordered otherwise`

@export How must I be paid while I am on long service leave under Victoria's Long Service Leave Act 2018 (s 20)? As agreed before the leave starts; otherwise either in full when the leave starts, or in your usual pay cycle.
GIVEN `we agreed before the leave started` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer and you agreed, before the leave started, how and when you would be paid for it
GIVETH A `How I must be paid on leave`
`How must I be paid on leave` MEANS
    `s 20 -- how I must be paid on leave` `we agreed before the leave started`

@export My ordinary pay went up while I was on long service leave: how much extra must I be paid under Victoria's Long Service Leave Act 2018 (s 21)? The increase, from the time of the increase, for the rest of the leave; if you were paid in full or in advance, it is due when the leave period ends.
GIVEN `weekly pay before the increase` IS A NUMBER @desc Your weekly ordinary pay, in dollars, before the increase
      `weekly pay after the increase` IS A NUMBER @desc Your weekly ordinary pay, in dollars, after the increase
      `weeks of leave from the increase` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of your leave fall on or after the increase
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much extra for a pay rise on leave` MEANS
    `s 21 -- the extra pay for the increase` `weekly pay before the increase` `weekly pay after the increase` `weeks of leave from the increase`

@export If I take my long service leave at half pay, how many weeks can I take under Victoria's Long Service Leave Act 2018 (s 22)? Twice as many weeks, at half your ordinary pay.
GIVEN `weeks of leave` IS A NUMBER @desc The weeks of long service leave you would otherwise take on full pay
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How many weeks at half pay` MEANS
    `s 22 -- the weeks at half pay` `weeks of leave`

@export Must my employer grant my request to take long service leave at half pay for twice as long under Victoria's Long Service Leave Act 2018 (s 22)? Yes, unless it has reasonable business grounds for refusing.
GIVEN `the employer has reasonable business grounds` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer has reasonable business grounds for refusing (see s 3: no capacity or impractical to change other employees' arrangements, likely significant loss of efficiency or productivity, likely significant negative impact on customer service); the court decides if disputed
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must my employer grant half-pay leave` MEANS
    `s 22 -- my employer must grant half-pay leave` `the employer has reasonable business grounds`

§§ `When my employment ends or I die (ss 8, 9, 10, 34)`
-- A situation the person may not be in: ask "Is your employment ending, or has it ended?" first.

@export My employment is ending (or has ended): how much must I be paid for my long service leave under Victoria's Long Service Leave Act 2018 (s 9)? The full amount of your untaken entitlement, worked out as at the last day, is due and payable on that day; nothing is payable under the Act if you have not completed 7 years.
GIVEN `the day it is counted from` IS A DATE @desc The day your continuous employment with your employer is counted from
      `the last day` IS A DATE @desc The day your employment ends
      `weeks that do not count` IS A NUMBER @desc The total weeks of absence that do not count towards the length of your employment; 0 if none
      `weeks already taken` IS A NUMBER @desc The weeks of long service leave you have already taken in the period; 0 if none
      `weekly ordinary pay` IS A NUMBER @desc Your weekly ordinary pay, in dollars, as at the day your employment ends (see the ordinary pay question)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much must I be paid when my employment ends` MEANS
    `ss 9, 10 -- the full amount` `the day it is counted from` `the last day` `weeks that do not count` `weeks already taken` `weekly ordinary pay`

@export My employment has ended: was my long service leave paid on time under Victoria's Long Service Leave Act 2018 (s 9)? It is due and payable in full on the day the employment ends, and the employer's obligation (an offence each day it continues) lasts until it is paid.
GIVEN `the amount owed` IS A NUMBER @desc The full amount, in dollars, owed for your long service leave (see the question on how much you must be paid)
      `the day my employment ended` IS A DATE @desc The day your employment ended
      `I have been paid in full` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have now been paid the full amount
      `the day I was paid in full` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day the full amount was paid (otherwise any day)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A `Whether my long service leave was paid on time`
`Was my long service leave paid on time` MEANS
    `s 9 -- whether I was paid on time` `the amount owed` `the day my employment ended` `I have been paid in full` `the day I was paid in full` `today`

@export May I accept a payment instead of taking my long service leave under Victoria's Long Service Leave Act 2018 (s 34)? No, unless it is your payment when your employment ends or another Act or your award or agreement permits it; accepting one otherwise is an offence (12 penalty units).
GIVEN `it is my payment when my employment ends` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the payment is the payment of your entitlement when your employment ends (s 9)
      `another Act or my fair work instrument permits it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether another Act, or your award or enterprise agreement, permits the payment
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`May I accept a payment instead of leave` MEANS
    `s 34 -- I may accept a payment in lieu` `it is my payment when my employment ends` `another Act or my fair work instrument permits it`

@export I am the personal representative of an employee who died before taking all their long service leave: how much must their employer pay me under Victoria's Long Service Leave Act 2018 (s 10)? The full amount still owed, worked out on their pay at the time of death (averages over the 52 weeks before death).
GIVEN `the day it is counted from` IS A DATE @desc The day the employee's continuous employment with the employer is counted from
      `the day of death` IS A DATE @desc The day the employee died
      `weeks that do not count` IS A NUMBER @desc The total weeks of absence that do not count towards the length of their employment; 0 if none
      `weeks already taken` IS A NUMBER @desc The weeks of long service leave they had already taken in the period; 0 if none
      `weekly ordinary pay at death` IS A NUMBER @desc Their weekly ordinary pay, in dollars, at the time of death: their normal weekly hours at their ordinary rate, with any averages taken over the 52 weeks before death
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much must be paid to the estate` MEANS
    `ss 9, 10 -- the full amount` `the day it is counted from` `the day of death` `weeks that do not count` `weeks already taken` `weekly ordinary pay at death`

§§ `Agreements that cut my leave (ss 23, 47, 49, 50)`

@export Does a term of my employment agreement, or of a deed (such as a settlement deed), that reduces or excludes my long service leave have any effect under Victoria's Long Service Leave Act 2018 (s 23)? Such a term is of no effect, unless the Industrial Division of the Magistrates' Court considers the agreement's long service leave more favourable than the Act's.
GIVEN `the term annuls, varies or excludes the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the term annuls, varies or excludes any provision of the Act (or of the 1992 Act), in an employment agreement or in a deed or agreement with your employer made before, during or after your employment
      `the court considers the agreement more favourable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Industrial Division of the Magistrates' Court is of the opinion that the long service leave under the agreement or deed is more favourable than under the Act; answer no if no such opinion has been given
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does a term cutting my leave have effect` MEANS
    `s 23 -- the term can have effect` `the term annuls, varies or excludes the Act` `the court considers the agreement more favourable`

@export Am I entitled to a better long service leave entitlement from an old award, instead of the Act's, under Victoria's Long Service Leave Act 2018 (s 47)? Yes, if an award binding your employer and covering your employment immediately before 27 March 2006 gave long service leave more beneficial in any respect than the 1992 Act.
GIVEN `an award applied to my employer and my employment before 27 March 2006` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an award (under the Workplace Relations Act 1996) bound your employer, and covered your employment, immediately before 27 March 2006, or would have if you or they had been in the industry then
      `it was more beneficial in any respect than Part 5 of the 1992 Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that award's long service leave was more beneficial to you in any respect than Part 5 of the Long Service Leave Act 1992
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Am I entitled to an old award's better leave` MEANS
    `s 47 -- I am entitled to the superior award entitlement` `an award applied to my employer and my employment before 27 March 2006` `it was more beneficial in any respect than Part 5 of the 1992 Act`

@export Do I keep long service leave that accrued under an award or agreement that has since ended or stopped applying, under Victoria's Long Service Leave Act 2018 (ss 48, 49)?
GIVEN `it accrued under an award or agreement that ended or stopped applying in one of the s 48 ways` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the leave accrued under an award that was later varied, set aside, ceased to have effect, revoked or stopped applying to you under the Workplace Relations Act 1996, or under an agreement that was later terminated or stopped applying to you under that Act
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Do I keep my protected accrued leave` MEANS
    `s 49 -- I keep my protected accrued entitlement` `it accrued under an award or agreement that ended or stopped applying in one of the s 48 ways`

@export Before an agreement that cuts my long service leave was made, did my employer tell me in time under Victoria's Long Service Leave Act 2018 (s 50)? It must notify you in writing at least 7 days before, saying whether the agreement modifies or removes the 7-year entitlement or a preserved award or accrued entitlement.
GIVEN `the agreement modifies or removes my entitlements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employment agreement would modify or remove your entitlements under the Act
      `I was notified in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer notified you in writing of the modification or removal
      `the notice stated what was modified or removed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the notice said whether the agreement modifies or removes the entitlement on completing 7 years, and any entitlement preserved by s 47 or s 49
      `the day of the notice` IS A DATE @desc The day you were notified
      `the day of the agreement` IS A DATE @desc The day the agreement was entered into
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Was I told in time about an agreement cutting my leave` MEANS
    `s 50 -- I was notified in time` `the agreement modifies or removes my entitlements` `I was notified in writing` `the notice stated what was modified or removed` `the day of the notice` `the day of the agreement`

§§ `Recovering what I am owed (ss 24, 26, 27, 36, 37)`
-- A situation the person may not be in: ask "Is your employer refusing to pay, or has it acted against you?" first.

@export By when must I start a proceeding to recover long service leave money my employer owes me under Victoria's Long Service Leave Act 2018 (s 26)? Within 6 years after the entitlement to the money arises, in the Industrial Division of the Magistrates' Court, after giving the employer a written demand; your union may sue for you.
GIVEN `the day the entitlement arose` IS A DATE @desc The day your entitlement to the money arose (for leave owed when employment ends, the day it ended)
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I sue for my long service leave money` MEANS
    `s 26(4) -- the last day to commence` `the day the entitlement arose`

@export Is my proceeding to recover long service leave money in time under Victoria's Long Service Leave Act 2018 (s 26)? It must be started within 6 years after the entitlement arises, and only after a written demand to the employer.
GIVEN `the day the entitlement arose` IS A DATE @desc The day your entitlement to the money arose (for leave owed when employment ends, the day it ended)
      `the day I commence` IS A DATE @desc The day you start (or plan to start) the proceeding
      `I gave a written demand first` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you (or your union) gave the employer a written demand for the money before starting
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is my claim for long service leave money in time` MEANS
    `s 26 -- my proceeding is in time` `the day the entitlement arose` `the day I commence` `I gave a written demand first`

@export Can the court order my employer to pay interest on the long service leave money it owes me under Victoria's Long Service Leave Act 2018 (s 26(6), (7))? Yes, if the court is satisfied the employer had reasonable notice, no reasonable grounds to dispute, and should have paid without a proceeding; the rate cannot exceed the penalty interest rate.
GIVEN `reasonable notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court is satisfied your employer had reasonable notice of your claim
      `no reasonable grounds to dispute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court is satisfied your employer had no reasonable grounds to dispute the claim
      `should have paid without a proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court is satisfied your employer should, in the circumstances, have paid without a proceeding being needed
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I be awarded interest` MEANS
    `s 26(6) -- interest may be ordered` `reasonable notice` `no reasonable grounds to dispute` `should have paid without a proceeding`

@export Did my employer take unlawful adverse action against me over my long service leave under Victoria's Long Service Leave Act 2018 (s 36)? An employer must not dismiss, injure, prejudice, discriminate against or misrepresent your entitlements to an employee because they are entitled to, seek, ask about or go to court over long service leave; the employer must prove its reason was not one of these.
GIVEN `what was done` IS A `What my employer did` @desc What your employer did: dismissed you; injured you in your employment; altered your position to your prejudice; discriminated between you and other employees; knowingly or recklessly misrepresented your long service leave entitlements; or none of these
      `the reason` IS A `The reason I say it was done` @desc The reason you say it was done: because you are entitled to long service leave or another entitlement under the Act; because you sought to exercise your entitlement; because you enquired about your entitlement; because you applied to the court about a direction to take leave; or no such reason
      `my employer proves it was not for that reason` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer has proved that the action was not taken for that reason (answer no if it has not)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Did my employer take unlawful adverse action against me` MEANS
    `s 36 -- my employer took unlawful adverse action against me` `what was done` `the reason` `my employer proves it was not for that reason`

@export I was dismissed in breach of the adverse action rule and reinstatement is impracticable: what is the most compensation the court can order under Victoria's Long Service Leave Act 2018 (s 27)? No more than your remuneration in the 52 weeks before the dismissal (the court can also order reimbursement of lost pay or reinstatement).
GIVEN `the employer contravened s 36` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer was found to have contravened the adverse action rule (s 36)
      `it was my dismissal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the adverse action was your dismissal
      `the court considers reinstatement impracticable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court considers it would be impracticable to reinstate you
      `remuneration in the 52 weeks before dismissal` IS A NUMBER @desc Your remuneration, in dollars, in the 52 weeks immediately before the dismissal
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What is the most compensation for my dismissal` MEANS
    `s 27(2) -- the most compensation` `the employer contravened s 36` `it was my dismissal` `the court considers reinstatement impracticable` `remuneration in the 52 weeks before dismissal`

@export May I work for pay during my long service leave under Victoria's Long Service Leave Act 2018 (s 35)? Not for hire or reward in the hours of your leave; doing so is an offence (12 penalty units).
GIVEN `the work is for hire or reward` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the work is paid (for hire or reward)
      `it is in the hours of my leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the work is in the hours during which you are taking long service leave
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`May I work for pay during my leave` MEANS
    `s 35 -- I may do the work` `the work is for hire or reward` `it is in the hours of my leave`

@export Must my employer still keep my long service leave record under Victoria's Long Service Leave Act 2018 (s 37(2), (3))? Throughout your continuous employment, and for at least 7 years after you stop working there.
GIVEN `I still work there` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you still work for the employer
      `the day I stopped working there` IS A DATE @desc If not, the day you stopped working for the employer (otherwise any day)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must my employer still keep my record` MEANS
    `s 37(2), (3) -- my employer must still keep my record` `I still work there` `the day I stopped working there` `today`

@export Must my employer give me a copy of my long service leave record under Victoria's Long Service Leave Act 2018 (s 37(6))? It must not refuse your request (or your personal representative's).
GIVEN `I have asked for a copy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you (or your personal representative) have asked your employer for a copy of your long service leave record
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must my employer give me a copy of my record` MEANS
    `s 37(6) -- my employer must give me a copy of my record` `I have asked for a copy`
